<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Signed macOS builds run under the hardened runtime, which notarization requires. It blocks
    the microphone unless the app says it uses it, and then macOS never even asks.
    This is the hardened-runtime key for an app outside the App Sandbox, which Oversay is not in
    (it writes the AI skill into ~/.claude and ~/.agents). The sandbox's own microphone key is
    not needed.

    Add nothing here without a reason: Oversay needs no JIT, unsigned-memory or
    library-validation exception, and no network or file-access entitlements.
    tauri.conf.json (bundle.macOS.entitlements) applies this file to everything it signs.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
